        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>OpenAI has launched a new security feature in ChatGPT called <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001061-lockdown-mode\">Lockdown Mode</a>, designed to provide additional protection against so-called \u201cprompt injection attacks.\u201d</p>\n\n\n\n<p>A prompt injection attack is when someone crafts a deceptive prompt in an attempt to trick the LLM into following malicious instructions and/or revealing sensitive information.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>These deceptive prompts are often hidden within web pages and other data sources, which are easily missed by humans but still read and processed by LLMs. Prompt injection attacks have been used to do all sorts of things, like <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/2885371/perplexitys-ai-browser-is-a-sucker-for-blatant-scams-and-prompt-hijacks.html\">hijacking Perplexity\u2019s AI browser</a>, <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/28",
